From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 04:33:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: a native child's freed RWX memory gives its JIT-pool
 range back

A MEM_RELEASE retired the anonymous JIT alias of the memory it freed but
kept its pool range until the process exited. In a native ARM64 child an
alias retired whole now puts its range on the pool's free list, after the
usual grace period, when the ledger still records it whole for the
process that allocated it (ios_pool_return_anon_locked). The free list
insertion is shared with the exit-time reclaim.

A native child's live anonymous executable memory is also held to a
quarter of the pool: past it the child's own allocation fails, instead of
a guest that leaks such memory exhausting the pool, which ends the launch
for every process.

Linear: PLA-514
Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-31-wow-arm64-start.md, tools/tests/test_x64_syscall_stub.py
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 144 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 114 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

